Falsifies `non_volatile_memory_express::verification::identify_parse_is_total_and_bounds_the_shift`.

The defect: `parse_identify_namespace` widens the accepted LBA data size from `9..=12` to `9..=13`.
An 8 KiB logical block then reaches `blocks_per_transfer(4096)`, which cannot serve it.

Expected to fail: the harness's `assert!((9..=12).contains(&id.logical_block_address_shift))`.

diff --git a/crates/non_volatile_memory_express/src/identify.rs b/crates/non_volatile_memory_express/src/identify.rs
index 2af30a051..c82b922cc 100644
--- a/crates/non_volatile_memory_express/src/identify.rs
+++ b/crates/non_volatile_memory_express/src/identify.rs
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@ pub fn parse_identify_namespace(data: &[u8]) -> Option<IdentifyNamespace> {
     let flbas = data[26] & 0xf;
     // LBA format `flbas` is 4 bytes at 128 + 4*flbas; LBADS is its third byte.
     let lbads = data[128 + 4 * flbas as usize + 2];
-    if !(9..=12).contains(&lbads) {
+    if !(9..=13).contains(&lbads) {
         return None;
     }
     Some(IdentifyNamespace {
